# AC4 — cache-hit within 60min TTL (NEARS-2989), positive control per NEARS-1856(c)

Instrument: MySQL general_log (temporarily enabled, `SET GLOBAL general_log=ON`, truncated between
calls, turned back OFF after), grepped for the aggregate's signature text.

$ php artisan cache:clear
$ mysql -e "TRUNCATE mysql.general_log"   # clean log

=== CALL 1 (cold cache) ===
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8091/api/v1/most-tips
{"most_tips_amount":40}
$ grep -ic "group by dm_tips" mysql_general.log
2   <- POSITIVE CONTROL: the aggregate query DID fire on the cold-cache call (channel proven live)

=== truncate log, CALL 2 (warm cache, same TTL window) ===
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8091/api/v1/most-tips
{"most_tips_amount":40}
$ grep -ic "group by dm_tips" mysql_general.log
0   <- second call: query did NOT fire, served from Cache::remember (60min TTL)

Same value (40) returned both times. Query fired once (call 1), silent on call 2 -- the silence is
meaningful because call 1 already proved the log channel captures the query when it does run
(NEARS-1856(c) positive-control requirement satisfied).
